# Split from server.lang - dialogue bundle (aetherhaven_dialogue_elder)
# Full translation keys are aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.<lineKey> (see Hytale I18nModule).
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gold_explainer.body=Gold can be earned by completing quests, found through exploration in chests and caches throughout the world, within ruins and other ancient locations. The town maintains its own treasury. Once the town hall is built, the treasury will be located inside it. Every morning, a small daily tax from our residents contributes to that fund, distinct from visitors passing through. The amount depends on their condition: if they are fed, rested, and in decent spirits, we receive more. If they are hungry, tired, or anxious, we receive less. Use the block there to deposit your own gold or withdraw town funds if the charter permits.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gold_explainer.c0=Good to know. Thanks.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gold_explainer.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.inn_done.body=There. A proper inn for proper folk. Corin has arrived and he will be your innkeeper. Go say hello by the hearth. You have earned more than a simple thank you from me, but that is all I can offer right now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.inn_done.c0=Happy to help.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.inn_done.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_accepted.body=When the house is complete, use the bookshelf inside and register me as the resident. Then come find me. I'll be here in the meantime.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_accepted.c0=I'll get to work.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_accepted.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_finish.body=Then we are finished. I have a roof same as anyone else here. Thank you for finding a place for me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_finish.c0=Welcome home, Lyren.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_finish.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_offer.body=The town hall is built, the charter is successsful, and we have a treasury inside it. If I can trouble you, I want the same small house anyone else receives. Here.  Take this token and stake the plot with your placement staff, pay the materials and the town share from the treasury, and then register my name on the bookshelf once built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_offer.c0=I'll handle it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_offer.c1=I cannot commit to that yet.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_offer.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_remind.body=Take the time you need. When the house is finished, register me on the management block, then come find me in person.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_remind.c0=I'll come when it is done.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.lyren_house_remind.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.quest_accepted.body=Good. If you haven't already, get a plot placement staff from the town planning desk and take this schematic for the inn. Choose a site to stake the plot, use the staff, provide the materials listed on the sign, and you're underway. You need not do anything else; it finishes by itself, though it takes time. If you want it faster, craft a Building Wand at the town planning desk and apply it to the green markers. When the building is finished, come see me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.quest_accepted.c0=I'll start as soon as I can.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.quest_accepted.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.remind_inn.body=When the inn is finished, with the roof complete and the hearth functional, come tell me in person. I am not leaving until this town has beds for travelers. The inn will build itself if you leave it undisturbed, or you can speed it up with a Building Wand if you possess one.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.remind_inn.c0=I'll come back when it is ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.remind_inn.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.rep_reward_100.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.rep_reward_50.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.body=A new town charter stands! I am Lyren, and I am here to help you. Let's not get caught up on where I came from or how I got here so quickly. We can talk about that later. For now, keeping people safe is our first priority, so I would ask that we first build an inn with a solid roof, a warm hearth, and a door that stays open to weary travelers. 
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c0=I'm in. Let's raise the inn.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c1=The inn is still on my list. I wanted to check in.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c10=I'll leave you to it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c2=The inn is finished. Corin should have what he needs.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c3=About the town hall.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c4=I put your name on the shelf.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c5=Your house is not done yet, but I am on it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c6=You mentioned wanting a house of your own.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c7=The town hall build is still underway.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c8=The town hall is up.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c9=How do people get gold coins around here?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_accepted.body=Use the town hall token with your staff, pay the materials, and let it build out. It will finish on its own. Craft a Building Wand at the town planning desk if you want to speed it up, then apply it to the green markers. When the hall is complete, come tell me in person.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_accepted.c0=I'll tell you the moment it is finished.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_accepted.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_done.body=There. We now have a town hall: records, a treasury, and a room where we can meet out of the cold. That is what I needed from you. Thank you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_done.c0=Glad it helps.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_done.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_offer.body=The inn is done. Next we need a town hall for everyone: a shelf for the charter, a desk for plans, and a treasury so town coin can pay for what we build together. Stake the plot with your staff and pay what the sign asks in materials. The hall will build itself over time if you wait. If you want it faster, craft a Building Wand at the town planning desk and use it on the green markers.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_offer.c0=I'll put the hall up.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_offer.c1=Not yet.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_offer.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_remind.body=Building takes time. The hall will finish without a Building Wand if you simply wait. When it is done, tell me. I will be here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_remind.c0=Still working on it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.town_hall_remind.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_offer.body=The hall is up and the treasury works. Folk beyond the sky should see what we are building, not only hear about it. A tourist portal draws travelers through each day. They wander our shops and stalls, spend coin, and some may decide to stay. Stake the plot with your staff, pay what the sign asks, and let the build run. When the portal is finished, come tell me yourself.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_offer.c0=I'll put the portal up.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_offer.c1=Not yet.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_offer.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_accepted.body=Use the portal token with your staff and pay the materials. It will finish on its own if you wait. Craft a Building Wand at the town planning desk if you want it faster. When travelers can step through, come find me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_accepted.c0=I'll tell you when it is ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_accepted.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_remind.body=The portal build takes time like any other plot. It will finish without a wand if you are patient. When it is done, tell me in person.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_remind.c0=Still working on it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_remind.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_done.body=Good. Let them come and look around. A town that only feeds itself is a camp. A town that welcomes strangers is becoming something real.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_done.c0=Glad to help.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.tourist_portal_done.speaker=Elder Lyren
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c11=About welcoming visitors.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c12=The tourist portal is still being built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c13=The tourist portal is finished.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.root.c14=About the foundation stones I brought you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.board.foundation_stones_thanks.body=Good work on the foundation stones. That haul will go straight into the next walls and paths we raise. Keep an eye on the board when you have time. There is always stone to move or timber to stack.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.board.foundation_stones_thanks.c0=Glad it helped.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gift.love=Thank you. A gift like that means something here for our survival.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gift.like=That was kind of you. Thank you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gift.neutral=Thank you. I will take it in the same spirit as it was given.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.gift.dislike=Alas, this is not for me. Perhaps next time something that fits the town's needs better.

aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.fallback=If you want to discuss the hall, the charter, or guidance on the town's direction, I can help.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.0=The hall still smells like ink and old wood. That keeps me steady during difficult times.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.1=I will keep the town hall tidy and answer any questions I can.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.2=Every choice has a consequence. Plan and execute carefully and all will be well.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.3=Everyone deserves a fair chance at survival. I hope we can provide that here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.4=A town this small shouldn't need so much paperwork. Oh, hello!
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.5=If gold goes missing from our coffers, you may need to review the charter. Someone may be stealing.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.6=The inn is great for short-term affairs, but everyone thrives when they have a home of their own.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.7=I used to be an adventurer like you. But then I got old, retired, and ended up here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.8=Someone left a note saying that we should hire a carter to move goods around town. We should talk about that later.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.greeting.9=Spend enough time with the villagers and they'll tell you what they like and don't like.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.love.0=Books and maps earn a smile from me faster than most trinkets.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.love.1=If you honor the charter in what you bring, I notice the gesture immediately.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.love.2=I could use a clean ink set or a solid shelf for the town hall.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.love.3=Founders' work and honest ledgers belong in the same sentence. Gifts can demonstrate that connection.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.love.4=I like bread and cheese as much as the next man. With luck, I will be the next man.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=I do not want grave goods or bone clutter in the hall. Respect the living town.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Keep street trash and random rubble out of my office basket.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.dislike.2=If an item belongs in a gutter, leave it there.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.dislike.3=Cheap junk jewelry does not impress me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_elder.main_hub.hint.dislike.4=I cannot stand the sight or the smell of spoiled food. Corin runs a clean kitchen, but I have known some really gross people in my day.